[%cachewrite 1859] The black rook on b9 attacks my cannon on b2, and nothing
protects that cannon. I can't just move the cannon away: once it leaves the
b-file, the rook can go straight down and take my horse on b0. I'll advance
that horse to c2 instead (马八进七). This protects the cannon, because my
central cannon on e2 can then fire along row 2 using the horse on c2 as a
screen. If the black rook takes on b2, I recapture with the e2 cannon and trade
a cannon for a rook, which favours me. The cannon on b2 also still blocks the
b-file, so the rook can't come down to b0. } 车２进６ 8. 炮八平九 {
