[%out 2857] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 1929] The black cannon on e3
has just advanced and is a real threat. It can use my cannon on e2 as a screen
to hit the knight on e1. That knight is holding things together: - It blocks
the file in front of my king, so my e2 cannon can't leave the file. - It is the
only piece protecting my knight on c2. My knight on c2 can capture the cannon
on e3: its leg point d2 is empty, so the move is legal. If the black rook on c3
recaptures, it is an even trade of knight for cannon. After that the rook would
sit on e3, right in front of my e2 cannon. The e2 cannon is covered by both
bishops, so there is no danger. If black instead grabs the c0 bishop with the
rook, I come out ahead in material. Removing this cannon first also frees my e2
cannon. } 车３平５ 11. 炮五平七 { [%emt 0:00:43] [%think 3497] [%out 3680]
