炮五平七 { [%emt 0:01:41] [%think 8401] [%out 8745] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0]
[%cachewrite 2090] The immediate danger is black's knight on g3. It can take my
undefended cannon on e2 with 马7进5. After that, knight checks from g1 or c1
are hard to meet, because my king is boxed in by the knight on e1 and both
advisors. Playing 炮五平七 (e2c2) solves several problems at once: 1. **The
cannon gets out of danger.** On c2 it is protected by my knight on e1, since
the knight's leg square d1 is empty. 2. **It blocks the black rook.** The rook
on c3 can no longer hit my elephant on c0 along the c-file. If the rook takes
the cannon, my knight recaptures and I win a rook for a cannon. 3. **It shuts
the knight out of e2.** If black's knight goes to e2, my a2 cannon captures it
by jumping over the c2 cannon, because d2 is empty. 4. **It frees my knight.**
With e2 empty, the e1 knight can later go to d3 or f3, which also opens e1 as
an escape square for my king. } 车３平５ 18. 炮七进五 { [%emt 0:01:01]
