[%out 5672] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2281] The immediate danger is
that Black threatens 车4退6 (d7d1): once the rook reaches d1, the rook on f1
can capture the knight on e1 with the d1 rook protecting it. My king has no
square to go to and my advisors cannot recapture on e1, so that would be mate.
So I move the knight from e1 to c2. From c2 it guards e1 (the d2 leg is empty).
If Black then plays d7d1 and takes on e1, I can recapture with the knight or
the king in turn. Black would lose two rooks and I would lose only one knight.
Other moves don't stop the mate: - 车二进一 (h0h1) hangs the rook: the black
rook on f1 can take it along the first rank. - 相五进三 (e2g4) wins a pawn but
does nothing against d7d1. } 马７进８ 26. 相五进三 { [%emt 0:00:46]
